{
  "changelog": "Major update: Adds a full data analysis pipeline alongside the experiment pipeline. Sub-skills expand from 3 to 6 (7 total with orchestrator).\n\n- Added data analysis workflow: psy-ana-designer (5-phase progressive design, 12-dimension method comparison, references 60 statistical methods and 48 chart types), psy-ana-coder (R and Python code generation, 12-step annotated script structure, 10-item quality gate), and psy-ana-reviewer (4 review modes, 5-dimension reproducibility audit, R 8 + Python 13 anti-pattern grep patterns).\n- Renamed experiment sub-skills from psych-experiment-programming/coder/code-reviewer to psy-exp-designer/coder/reviewer, unifying the psy- prefix and -designer/-coder/-reviewer suffix convention across both chains.\n- Dual-chain routing: orchestrator now distinguishes experiment requests from analysis requests by intent, routes to the correct chain, and supports cross-chain bridging (completed experiment \u2192 analysis entry). Ambiguous requests trigger clarification.\n- Recovery Loop: both reviewers upgraded from single-pass audit to check \u2192 fix \u2192 re-audit cycle. Each issue maps to a repair path routing back to the appropriate coder. Cycle repeats until zero Critical + zero Major.\n- Trigger keywords expanded to cover 5-language analysis and statistical workflows (\u4e2d\u6587/English/\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e/Deutsch/Fran\u00e7ais).\n- All internal cross-references, READMEs, and orchestrator routing tree updated for the 7-skill dual-pipeline structure.",
